</style></head><body><h1>IRC channel logs</h1><h2>2024-09-10.log</h2><p><a href="/bootstrappable">back to list of logs</a></p><div id="logs"><div class="line" id="031346"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#031346" label="[03:13:46]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">cosinusoidally: neat</span></div><div class="line" id="054849"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#054849" label="[05:48:49]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">cosinusoidally: hmmm! interesting</span></div><div class="line" id="113638"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#113638" label="[11:36:38]">&lt;pabs3&gt;</a></span><span class="message"> <a rel="nofollow" href="https://codeberg.org/stagex/stagex">https://codeberg.org/stagex/stagex</a> </span></div><div class="line" id="114223"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#114223" label="[11:42:23]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">isn't that lrvick's project?</span></div><div class="line" id="114248"><span class="nick" style="color:#8dd3c7"><a href="#114248" label="[11:42:48]">&lt;fossy&gt;</a></span><span class="message">looks it</span></div><div class="line" id="115155"><span class="nick" style="color:#2e2a4a"><a href="#115155" label="[11:51:55]">&lt;pabs3&gt;</a></span><span class="message">yep</span></div><div class="line" id="215912"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#215912" label="[21:59:12]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">I started it but 5ish active contributors now so no longer &quot;mine&quot; ^_^</span></div><div class="line" id="220719"><span class="nick" style="color:#80b1d3"><a href="#220719" label="[22:07:19]">&lt;stikonas&gt;</a></span><span class="message">well, it always helps a project to have multiple contributors</span></div><div class="line" id="230326"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#230326" label="[23:03:26]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">lrvick: congrats on software success (any project with more than 1 developer is the definition of software success)</span></div><div class="line" id="230431"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#230431" label="[23:04:31]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">And being used in produduction by two companies who can't risk trusting any single release engineer, so there is incentive to keep supporting and improving it.</span></div><div class="line" id="230443"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#230443" label="[23:04:43]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">Also used heavily by my own company, so technically 3 so far</span></div><div class="line" id="230505"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#230505" label="[23:05:05]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">it is also the basis of airgapos, which is used by a few more</span></div><div class="line" id="230525"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#230525" label="[23:05:25]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">so yeah... now I am obligated to keep it maintained...</span></div><div class="line" id="230640"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#230640" label="[23:06:40]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">we have a couple hacks in our bootstrapping flow, like to work around ungz symlinks, and an much older live-bootstrap. I hope to take another pass at that soonish.</span></div><div class="line" id="230750"><span class="nick" style="color:#6b8072"><a href="#230750" label="[23:07:50]">&lt;lrvick&gt;</a></span><span class="message">but the entire tree is 100% deterministic, and a drop-in-replacement for most projects using alpine to build in containers today for most major languages.</span></div><div class="line" id="235420"><span class="nick" style="color:#389600"><a href="#235420" label="[23:54:20]">&lt;oriansj&gt;</a></span><span class="message">lrvick: nice.</span></div><br /></div></body></html>